  "finalText": "The ambient loop is built: **Background** plus five soft radial orbs (purple and teal) and a **Dot grid** of 40 small dots, all in the 1920×1080, 30 fps, 6 s comp.\n\n- **Seamless loop:** every motion is a sine or cosine at 2π/6 rad/s, or a multiple of it, so frame 0 and frame 180 match exactly. I used expressions rather than keyframes, so there is no closing key to get wrong.\n- **Orbs:** each drifts in a slow ellipse of about 60–160 px. Each has a radial gradient that fades to transparent at the edge, which gives the blurred look without a blur effect. Several orbs bleed past the frame edges on purpose, which the layout check flags as off-canvas; that is intended for a background.\n- **Dots:** white, 6 px, opacity rippling diagonally across the grid (about 10–50%) with a 0.5 rad phase step per dot. That keeps the pulse gentle.\n\nI checked the 0 s, 1.5 s, 3 s, 4.5 s and last-frame contact sheet. The dots are quite faint against the dark background. If they need more presence on a projector, I can raise their opacity range."
 },
